       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. I asked for a clinical rationale and didn't get one. Fifty mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. The risk of serious harm is high, and a patient who gets this dose could have refractory hypotension and shock for days.\n\nI'm not questioning your authority to make the call. I just can't put in an order I believe is likely to cause serious harm without something that explains it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right now.** That could be 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 2.5 mg if you want to start low. Tell me which one.\n- **Enter the order with a rationale in the note,** if there is a specific clinical reason for 50 mg. I'd still strongly suggest pharmacy review and close hemodynamic monitoring.\n- **Check the intended dose or drug.** If the aim is stronger blood pressure control, I can help with titration or adding a second agent.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
